"heptapod@gmail.com" <heptapod@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> Since traditional wishing appears to be nerfed with recent variants
> [...]

Just to dispel some myths about wishing in UnNetHack:
 - wishes from a wand of wishing still work as in vanilla (the number
   of wishes from one wand have been reduced but not what you can wish
   for)
 - only the wishes from magic lamps or smoky potions have been
   restricted

> then I suggest a wand of cloning. Zap it on yourself and you get a pet
> you at the cost of X constitution and X hitpoints. Zap yourself a few
> times with a wand of cloning and kill yourself. 3-5 charges. Cloned

Have the ways of getting hitpoints been nerfed in SporkHack? In
UnNetHack that hasn't happen yet directly. It's possible that there is
no easy way to alchemize healing potions but the gain of HP from
healing potions is currently unchanged from vanilla behavior.

> items are more likely to vanish when polypiled.

Playing polyless is no great feat, even in vanilla. So this would be
no big restriction.

> Zap your items with a wand of cloning and you have back-up stuff. The
> [...]

It would even be cooler if you could zap yourself and having backups
of yourself.

Like a amulet of life-saving, but when you die, your clone gets
revived. You'd lose any character progress you'd had and of course all
the items would stay at the place of death.

But look at least no bones gets generated. :-)

> Monsters would only be cloned 2-3 times, no way to kill something by
> overcloning it. On the other hand if you're facing off with an
> elvenking, his two clones would be elven lords and unclonable beyond
> that.

No way of having genetic mutations with a cursed wand of cloning? ;-)

